An informal term for Structural typing - if an object has the required methods/properties (\"quacks like a duck\"), it can be used regardless of its declared type or class hierarchy.

An informal term for ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/structural-typing.td")} - if an object has the required methods/properties ("quacks like a duck"), it can be used regardless of its declared type or class hierarchy.
